00:00:17.552 --> 00:00:18.930
Take a look.

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.780
- Hello, I'm Betty White.

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.150
- You're invited to experience

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:25.520
the amazing life of Betty
White on January 17th.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:26.353
- Betty White.

00:00:26.353 --> 00:00:27.186
- Betty White.

00:00:27.186 --> 00:00:28.019
- Betty White.

00:00:28.019 --> 00:00:28.860
- Betty White, ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:30.690
- Dorothy, was Sophia naked just now

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:32.599
or does her dress really need ironing?

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:33.638
(laughing)

00:00:33.638 --> 00:00:34.820
- Love her.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.490
The documentary was in the works

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:38.020
long before Betty's passing,

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:40.580
but it contains her last time on camera

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:43.740
recorded just 11 days
before the world lost her.

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.550
Joining us as the producer
and director of the film,

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:48.020
Steve Boettcher.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:48.853
Hi Steve.

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:50.893
- Hey Kelly,

00:00:50.893 --> 00:00:51.726
how are you?

00:00:51.726 --> 00:00:52.559
- I'm so good.

00:00:52.559 --> 00:00:54.530
I'm so sad we're talking
under these circumstances,

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:56.850
but I'm so glad at least y'all
were working on this project

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:59.580
and we have this like last little gift.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:01.930
All of America is devastated
by Betty's passing,

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:05.680
so what do you hope people take
away from your documentary?

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:07.040
- You know, we've been
working on this project

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.150
for about 10 years

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:10.180
and I didn't really realize
this was gonna be like

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:11.890
a love letter to Betty,

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:13.670
but I think at the end,
that's what this is.

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:15.920
It's a love letter to
Betty and her fans and

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:19.240
you know, it radiates her
heart and her happiness

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:22.290
and her humor and it's pure Betty White.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:23.123
- I love that.

00:01:23.123 --> 00:01:24.740
So you worked closely with
Betty on this project.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:27.100
So what did you come
to appreciate about her

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:28.840
that maybe we don't know?

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:31.390
- You know, it's that
razor sharp sense of humor,

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:33.930
that's Betty that I just,
you can't help, but love.

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:34.960
She always would say,

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:36.200
I be traveling with her,

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.270
we'd be arm and arm.

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:40.900
and she'd said, oh, by the
way, Steve Boettcher's with me,

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.780
he's been embedded with
me for the last 10 years.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:45.991
And she would wink when
she said it embedded with.

00:01:45.991 --> 00:01:46.824
(laughing)

00:01:46.824 --> 00:01:48.160
And it was just kind of like, you know,

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:49.795
I was always part of the
joke, you know what I mean?

00:01:49.795 --> 00:01:52.170
But by nature, she's a troublemaker,

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:53.620
her sense of humor is a troublemaker,

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:54.910
but I think it defines her

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:56.610
and you know, just kind of a rascal

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:57.443
and that's what I love about her.

00:01:57.443 --> 00:01:58.370
- I mean, yeah.

00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:00.300
What a life.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:03.300
Betty White: A Celebration
is in theaters nationwide

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:06.500
